      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "What are the radius $r$ and the coordinates of the center $C$ for the sphere $(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-3)^{2}=4?$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-(-2))^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-3)^{2}={2}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the center at the point point $C(-2,0,3)$ and the radius $r=2.$",
